  "goodToKnow": "Das Betäubungsmittel is a narcotic or anaesthetic. In law, the Betäubungsmittelgesetz (BtMG) regulates controlled drugs, and strong painkillers like morphine need a special BtM-Rezept. Since 2024, cannabis for adults is regulated separately and no longer under the BtMG. Betäuben means to anaesthetise or stun, from taub (deaf, numb). The plural is the same."
